        "original_id": "3f41c269-a803-5840-8dcf-ed830520ca7d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dean Martin\n- Products: Swingin' Down Yonder\n- Companies: Capitol Records\n- Topics: American entertainment, music recording\n\nFacts:\n- In September and October 1954 and February 1955, Dean Martin recorded Swingin' Down Yonder during three sessions for Capitol Records.\n- Swingin' Down Yonder was Dean Martin's first full-length 12-inch album for Capitol Records.\n- Dean Martin was one of the most popular and enduring American entertainers of the mid-20th century.\n- Dean Martin was nicknamed the \"King of Cool\" for his seemingly effortless charisma and self-assurance.",
